## Estimate: ~80 LOC

## Context
The Unicode research review concluded that full normalization/confusable pipelines are not a fit for this scanner, but BiDi control presence near matches is a cheap and meaningful risk signal. We should add this as a confidence signal in the hot-path scoring model without changing byte offsets or regex behavior.

## Current State
Confidence scoring is additive and currently only accounts for entropy, keyword presence, assignment shape, and offline structural validation.

```rust
// src/engine/window_validate.rs:468-489 — current score computation
fn compute_confidence_score(
    gates: &ResolvedGates<'_>,
    rule: &RuleCompiled,
    outcome: &EmitPolicyOutcome,
) -> i8 {
    let mut s: i8 = 0;
    if gates.entropy.is_some() {
        s = s.saturating_add(confidence::ENTROPY_PASS);
    }
    if gates.keywords.is_some() {
        s = s.saturating_add(confidence::KEYWORD_PRESENT);
    }
    if rule.needs_assignment_shape_check() {
        s = s.saturating_add(confidence::ASSIGNMENT_SHAPE);
    }
    if outcome.offline_verdict_valid {
        s = s.saturating_add(confidence::OFFLINE_VALID);
    }
    debug_assert!(s >= 0, "Phase 1 score must be non-negative: {s}");
    debug_assert!(s <= 10, "Phase 1 score exceeds max: {s}");
    s.clamp(0, 10)
}
```

Constants and compile-time guard assume a Phase 1 maximum of 10.

```rust
// src/api.rs:982-1001 — current confidence constants + max guard
pub mod confidence {
    pub const ENTROPY_PASS: i8 = 1;
    pub const KEYWORD_PRESENT: i8 = 2;
    pub const ASSIGNMENT_SHAPE: i8 = 2;
    pub const OFFLINE_VALID: i8 = 5;
}

const _: () = assert!(
    (confidence::ENTROPY_PASS as i16
        + confidence::KEYWORD_PRESENT as i16
        + confidence::ASSIGNMENT_SHAPE as i16
        + confidence::OFFLINE_VALID as i16)
        <= 10
);
```

The window-validation flow has no BiDi byte check today; step 14 computes confidence from existing gate presence only.

```text
// docs/engine-window-validation.md:34-64
[Gate 13] Apply offline structural validation ...
  ↓
[Step 14] Compute additive confidence score from gate signals that fired
```

## Desired State
Add a lightweight BiDi-control detector for candidate windows and contribute a new positive confidence signal (for example `BIDI_CONTEXT = +2`) when any target BiDi controls are present.

Target codepoints:
- `U+202A..U+202E` (embeddings/overrides)
- `U+2066..U+2069` (isolates)
- `U+200E`, `U+200F`, `U+061C`

Implementation must remain allocation-free and preserve current span/offset semantics.

