## Context
The Unicode security research plan in `~/.claude/plans/twinkling-sleeping-pizza.md` identified a concrete output-layer risk: bidirectional format controls can survive current sink sanitization and visually reorder rendered paths in terminals, SARIF viewers, and JSON consumers. This is a Trojan-Source-style presentation risk at the reporting boundary (not a byte-matching issue in the scanner core).

## Current State
`sanitize_path` in the text sink only escapes characters where `char::is_control()` is true; BiDi format controls are Unicode category `Cf` and are not treated as controls.

```rust
// src/unified/text_sink.rs:125-145 — control-only escaping
let lossy = String::from_utf8_lossy(bytes);
if !lossy.chars().any(char::is_control) {
    return lossy.into_owned();
}
for ch in lossy.chars() {
    if ch == '\u{FFFD}' {
        out.push(ch);
    } else if ch.is_control() {
        let cp = ch as u32;
        if cp <= 0xff {
            let _ = write!(&mut out, "\\x{cp:02x}");
        } else {
            let _ = write!(&mut out, "\\u{{{cp:04x}}}");
        }
    } else {
        out.push(ch);
    }
}
```

`write_json_bytes` only escapes JSON specials and C0 control bytes. Valid UTF-8 format characters (including BiDi overrides/isolates) pass through unchanged.

```rust
// src/unified/json_write.rs:533-563 — no Cf/BiDi handling
match b {
    b'"' | b'\\' | b'\n' | b'\r' | b'\t' | 0x00..=0x1f => {
        escape_json_byte(b, buf);
    }
    0x20..=0x7e => buf.push(b),
    _ => {
        let remaining = &bytes[i..];
        match std::str::from_utf8(remaining) {
            Ok(s) => {
                write_json_str(s, buf);
                return;
            }
            Err(e) => {
                let valid_up_to = e.valid_up_to();
                if valid_up_to > 0 {
                    let valid = unsafe { std::str::from_utf8_unchecked(&remaining[..valid_up_to]) };
                    write_json_str(valid, buf);
                    i += valid_up_to;
                    continue;
                }
                buf.extend_from_slice(b"\\u00");
                buf.push(HEX_DIGITS[(b >> 4) as usize]);
                buf.push(HEX_DIGITS[(b & 0xf) as usize]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

