### Numerical examples
- "abcdefghijklmnop" (sequential ASCII): SCC ~ +0.99 -> REJECTED
- "0123456789012345" (repeating digits): SCC ~ +0.87 -> REJECTED
- "aK9$mP2&xR5#nQ7@" (random-looking): SCC ~ +0.02 -> PASSES
- "ghp_x8Kj2mNpR4sV7wY" (real token): SCC ~ -0.05 -> PASSES

### Risk analysis
- False negatives: Some real secrets have mild serial correlation (e.g., base64 padding). Threshold of 0.25 is conservative.
- Integration: Runs on extracted secret bytes AFTER regex match. Cost is per-match, not per-window.

